      "message": "I think that `get_temp` can be static in shim/src/temp_sensors.c so it doesn\u0027t need to be in a new header. But as a general guideline we try to do things like:\n\n#ifndef __CROS_EC_TEMP_SENSOR_THERMISTOR_H\n#error \"Do not include this file directly, it is auto included from \"driver/temp_sensor/thermistor.h\"\n#endif\n\nThen in platform/ec/include/driver/temp_sensor/thermistor.h you add:\n\n#ifdef CONFIG_ZEPHYR\n#include \"driver/temp_sensor/zthermistor.h\"\n#endif\n\nThis way the zephyr specific header is hidden. When we go 100% zephyr we won\u0027t have to make any changes to the include sites.",
